#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1. Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend {#choose-a-backend}"
msgstr "Choose a backend {#choose-a-backend}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To detect errors during the circuit, we need to choose a backend that has access to the `MidCircuitMeasure` method (see the [documentation](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendeteksi kesalahan selama sirkuit berjalan, kita perlu memilih backend yang memiliki akses ke metode `MidCircuitMeasure` (lihat [dokumentasi](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a sequence of bit-flip stabilizer circuits implementing multiple rounds of error detection and correction {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"
msgstr "Build a sequence of bit-flip stabilizer circuits implementing multiple rounds of error detection and correction {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit-flip code is among the simplest examples of a stabilizer code. It protects the state against a single bit-flip (X) error on any of the encoding qubits. Consider the action of bit-flip error $X$, which maps $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ on any of our qubits, then we have $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. The code requires five qubits: three are used to encode the protected state (the \"data qubits\"), and the remaining two are used as stabilizer measurement ancillas.\n"
msgstr "Kode bit-flip adalah salah satu contoh kode stabilizer yang paling sederhana. Kode ini melindungi state dari satu kesalahan bit-flip (X) pada salah satu qubit encoding. Pertimbangkan aksi kesalahan bit-flip $X$, yang memetakan $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ pada salah satu qubit kita, maka kita punya $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. Kode ini memerlukan lima qubit: tiga digunakan untuk mengenkode state yang dilindungi (\"data qubits\"), dan dua sisanya digunakan sebagai ancilla pengukuran stabilizer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below you will build circuits that (1) prepare the data qubits in the logical $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$ state, then (2) run multiple cycles of a $5 \\mu s$ delay followed by error correction (including reset of the syndrome qubits), and (3) read out the state of the data qubits.\n"
msgstr "Di bawah ini kamu akan membangun sirkuit yang (1) menyiapkan qubit data dalam keadaan logis $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$, kemudian (2) menjalankan beberapa siklus delay $5 \\mu s$ diikuti dengan koreksi kesalahan (termasuk reset qubit sindrom), dan (3) membaca keadaan qubit data.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will also test the lifetime of the $|1\\rangle$ state without using error correction by including three reference qubits that we prepare in the $|1\\rangle$ state, leave idle, and then read out.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga akan menguji masa pakai keadaan $|1\\rangle$ tanpa menggunakan koreksi kesalahan dengan menyertakan tiga qubit referensi yang kita siapkan dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, biarkan idle, lalu dibaca.\n"

